{"name":"Cry of a Rose","hex":"#b23c5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Cori."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shed tears; to weep, especially in anger or sadness.","To utter loudly; to call out; to declare publicly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cry"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crying","blocks":[{"text":"Crying is the dropping of tears in response to an emotional state or physical pain. Emotions that can lead to crying include sadness, anger, joy, and fear. Crying can also be caused by relief from a period of stress or anxiety, or as an empathetic response. The act of crying has been defined as \"a complex secretomotor phenomenon characterized by the shedding of tears from the lacrimal apparatus, without any irritation of the ocular structures\", instead, giving a relief which protects from conjunctivitis. A related medical term is lacrimation, which also refers to the non-emotional shedding of tears. Various forms of crying are known as sobbing, weeping, wailing, whimpering, bawling, and blubbering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/330px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crying"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Ghanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two women weep at a funeral","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGhanian_Funeral_Rite_-_One_Week_Celebration_of_the_Dead_08_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Tears_.jpg/500px-Tears_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Tears_.jpg/1280px-Tears_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Tears_.jpg/500px-Tears_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Child crying","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATears_.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg/500px-D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg/1280px-D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg/500px-D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Queen Maria II of Portugal crying and hugging a bust of her late father King Pedro IV (also Emperor of Brazil as Pedro I), 1836","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AD._Maria_II_(BM_1868%2C0612.2285).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Crying_infant_%2843101898172%29.jpg/500px-Crying_infant_%2843101898172%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Crying_infant_%2843101898172%29.jpg/1280px-Crying_infant_%2843101898172%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Crying_infant_%2843101898172%29.jpg/500px-Crying_infant_%2843101898172%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut